<article class="env-lemma" id="01W5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01W5">Lemma <span data-tag="01W5">29.42.6</span>.</a> A closed immersion is proper, hence a fortiori universally closed. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The base change of a closed immersion is a closed immersion (Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01JY" data-tag="01JY">26.18.2</a>). Hence it is universally closed. A closed immersion is separated (Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01L7" data-tag="01L7">26.23.8</a>). A closed immersion is of finite type (Lemma <a href="/tag/01T5" data-tag="01T5">29.15.5</a>). Hence a closed immersion is proper. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>